# Classical UI is mandatory

Before any change that a teacher or student can see (layout, CSS, copy, overlay, dialog, form, empty state, Agent panel), read and obey `design-system/cdas-next/CLASSICAL.md`.

`design-system/cdas-next/MASTER.md` is a historical UI-201 draft. Do not copy its navy filled buttons, system sans-serif stack, or `#174ea6`. Live tokens live in `src/app/globals.css`.

Hard rules:

- Use existing CSS variables only. No new hex, font names, or spacing/type px in components.
- Interface counts use `--figure-ui` (lining + tabular) and `--font-ui` for large stats. Do not display Cormorant oldstyle figures.
- Buttons are stroked, not filled. Color is a stroke, not a slab.
- Callouts: transparent + divider + 2px left accent.
- Agent overlay: transcript is the primary surface; chrome stays thin; no page dimmer; no chat bubbles.
- Confirm high-impact writes with existing `ConfirmDialog` and existing domain commands.

If a visual choice is not in CLASSICAL.md or `globals.css`, do not invent it — extend CLASSICAL.md in the same change after matching existing screens.
